    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/5/75387.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 49,
    "turn_text": "Well, listen, I'll tell you what the appeasement was when Obama did nothing, when Russia entered Ukraine, a Crimea, and advanced in the Eastern Ukraine. You know, when Biden was saying a little incursion, it's OK, and was slow-working aid, and didn't even help them at the beginning or before the war. That's an appeasement. Putin didn't move on to Trump. Trump inherited all the situations. So I think he is going to try to stop at least them moving further. You know, we have to deal tough in Russia. We need to figure out, but at least we need to stop them of advances further because if we don't do something very soon, they might start advancing further. That's a reality because Europe be the peace in Russia by depending on their gas and oils, by having business relationships with Russia. They're putting real sanctions and doing a lot of loopholes. So let's just be honest. talk about that a lot of people are dying, but ballistic missiles are not landing in capitals in Europe. They don't see what destruction is happening. They don't see what's happening on the front line. So it is going to be on the temporary resolution, I think, of this issue. But at least you can stop Russia from moving further.",
