  {
    "episode_id": 75387,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/5/75387.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 51,
    "turn_text": "No, it's actually, you know, I grew up in the Soviet Union, and if you remember, Hayek said the biggest danger, the actual communism, the definition of centralized power of centralized government, and that's what happened. We centralized an enormous amount of power that we cannot do things that we should be doing well. We're doing too many things, and nothing is good. And we have a lot of problems everywhere. And we need to do better. We need to make sure that we have strong military national defense. We protect our border, have good interstate commerce, good economy, and protect our constitutional rights. That's what the federal government has created. And we need to go with significant reset, because as I said, it's like a Titanic. Some of my colleagues think we're You know, submarine, but unfortunately we are not. We are like a Titanic on the collision course. And if we want to avoid it, we need to have some big serious moves. And the line is trying to push some government, at least in some efficiency, but it's ultimately for the Congress to put it in the law. And that's what I'm working on.",
