    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/5/75387.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 52,
    "turn_text": "It's interesting that right now the Congress isn't really able to effectively push back against what Elon Musk and Doge is doing, but certainly federal judges and courts are pushing back. They've blocked him, for example, from having access to the vast treasury payment system, saying that they're operating in Doge in such a flawed and haphazard way that to give them control of treasury payments or access to treasury payments would likely be illegal. Now, Donald Trump and Elon Musk seem to be saying that if the courts continue to rule against them, they are going to take on the judges. Is America going to be a democracy if the executive branch starts to intimidate the courts and the judges?",
