    "turn_idx": 53,
    "turn_text": "We are a republic, actually not a democracy, a judicial system. Unfortunately, it's been broken and really stuck against people with no money. That's about the quality of rights. That was the strength of republic. And we don't have it. So the judicial system needs some work, but ultimately Congress is broken. Roughly 85% of our spending, the money, we never even looked at it. Think about it. It's automatics. We don't even look at it. And we barely look at the rest. Until Congress is doing this job, we cannot save this republic. But that job now of my party. We have control of the House and the Senate. That's why I need to work on making Republicans great again. I need to make sure that my party is going to deliver in the law great policies that President Trump tried to accomplish for the country.",
