  {
    "episode_id": 75387,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/5/75387.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 59,
    "turn_text": "You say that is your role, isn't your number one role, to defend democracy? You are in the legislative branch. You're an elected politician. And I just wonder whether you are worried that one of America's leading political scientists says that what he sees in these early weeks of Donald Trump's second term is a slide into a new model of autocracy. He calls it competitive authoritarianism. There are still going to be elections, he says, but incumbent abuse of power systematically tilts the playing field against the opposition in this new America. You should be fighting against that, shouldn't you?",
